he `renormalize` supersession pattern is documented in the\n-  spec as the mechanism should a future vocabulary change ever need one.\n-- **`ReadOptions` gains `tool`, `kind` widened to `string | string[]`, and\n-  `linkRel`** — each backed by cited consumer code, with `actorId`,\n-  `since`/`until`, and `producerVersion` deferred with reasons.\n-- **Registration is the consumer-discovery form**: persisted\n-  `{tool, kind, version, schema}` so a consumer can enumerate a ledger's\n-  third-party vocabularies instead of hardcoding them. Unregistered kinds stay\n-  storable; reads stay tolerant.\n-- **The `ensureTransport` side effect gets documented loudly** — appending a\n-  single event installs a pre-push hook and fetch refspec (`store.ts:172`).\n+For `turnbridge`'s `continuation` kind, `readLineage` and\n+`ContinuationRecord` are that public reader. Consumers such as context-graph\n+must import the reader rather than parse `content` themselves. The annals\n+filters needed by consumers (`kind: string | string[]`, `tool`, and `linkRel`)\n+are already available through cledger's unchanged public read surface.\n \n"}},"status":"completed","stderr":"","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge/docs/TODO_HANDOFF.md\n","success":true,"turn_id":"01a0d115-a509-7c00-bfb6-084d7f9753c0"},"context":{"branch":"continuation-source-events","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","head":"3c28c765c2c1653fc99494c6ea0ad2081f7b48f8","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"id":"ev2-c4eb4cd506748cb4af82ec76b342609e08749a8bde5593115eb4db01f3f391c8","kind":"activity","meta":{"actor":{"type":"system"},"model":"gpt-5.6-sol","provider":"openai","session_id":"375a062e-4769-4548-82b0-af1a929dc456","source":"codex","source_version":"0.156.1"},"occurred_at":"2026-09-24T01:45:24.760Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.26.0"},"raw":{"data":{"payload":{"call_id":"exec-3dd6bf3c-5fd5-404d-b84e-a209445e93df",