{"content":{"blocks":[{"content":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":" M docs/LINEAGE_AND_COMPOUNDING.md\n M docs/TODO_HANDOFF.md\n docs/LINEAGE_AND_COMPOUNDING.md | 21 +++++++++----------\n docs/TODO_HANDOFF.md            | 46 ++++++++++++++---------------------------\n 2 files changed, 25 insertions(+), 42 deletions(-)\ndiff --git a/docs/LINEAGE_AND_COMPOUNDING.md b/docs/LINEAGE_AND_COMPOUNDING.md\nindex 9e5fe61..74506bc 100644\n--- a/docs/LINEAGE_AND_COMPOUNDING.md\n+++ b/docs/LINEAGE_AND_COMPOUNDING.md\n@@ -6,9 +6,9 @@ model covers capture as well as write. This is that question followed all the\n way down: it turns out to be a three-repo architecture question spanning\n conversation-ledger, turnbridge, and context-graph.\n \n-Most of this is still undecided. The exception is §4, the cledger-side\n-extension governance, which is settled and now lives in that repo at\n-`docs/EXTENSION_GOVERNANCE.md` (branch `design/extension-governance`).\n+Most of this is still undecided. The exception is §4's extension-ownership\n+question, which is settled in annals' README: annals owns storage, while the\n+producer owns its vocabulary, versioning, and reader.\n \n ## 1. What \"actor identity\" means\n \n@@ -191,7 +191,7 @@ arithmetic, which is cheap but coarse — it identifies a *range*, and assumes\n positional correspondence survived the render. turnbridge knows more than that\n at fabricate time: it knows the exact ordered list of source event ids it\n rendered. Recording that list in the `continuation` event's content makes the\n-mapping precise (target position *i* ⟵ source event `ev1-…`) at essentially no\n+mapping precise (target position *i* ⟵ source event `ev2-…`) at essentially no\n cost, and needs no cledger change — `content` is uninterpreted by design.\n \n ## 3a. What the walk should actually do\n@@ -318,18 +318,17 @@ retrofitted front door, not a designed external-input API — though the append\n path behind 