{"content":{"blocks":[{"content":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"../annals/README.md-3-Append-only records anchored to git commits: typed, linkable, redacted on\n../annals/README.md-4-write, synced through git notes. annals is the storage layer extracted from\n../annals/README.md-5-[conversation-ledger](https://github.com/evintunador/conversation-ledger)\n../annals/README.md:6:(cledger), which now sits on top of it as one vocabulary among several.\n../annals/README.md-7-\n../annals/README.md-8-A record (\"event\") is a JSON object stored one-per-line in a git note attached\n../annals/README.md-9-to the commit that was `HEAD` when it happened. Because storage is git notes\n--\n../annals/README.md-16-annals owns **facts about records**: identity, dedup, ordering, links,\n../annals/README.md-17-commit anchoring, re-anchoring after squash merges, redaction on write, the\n../annals/README.md-18-pre-push secret scan, and transport. It never interprets `content` — what a\n../annals/README.md:19:record *means* belongs to the tool that wrote it (`producer.tool`), which\n../annals/README.md:20:owns that vocabulary, its versioning, and its reader.\n../annals/README.md-21-\n../annals/README.md:22:A third-party record kind is identified by the pair **`(producer.tool,\n../annals/README.md:23:kind)`**, never by `kind` alone. `producer.version` names the vocabulary\n../annals/README.md:24:revision. annals validates the envelope only; producers validate their own\n../annals/README.md-25-payloads in their own packages.\n../annals/README.md-26-\n../annals/README.md-27-## The envelope\n--\n../annals/README.md-30-{\n../annals/README.md-31-  id: \"ev2-<sha256 of the identity subset>\",\n../annals/README.md-32-  schema: \"annals/v1\",\n../annals/README.md:33:  kind: string,                    // open; owned by (producer.tool, kind)\n../annals/README.md-34-  occurred_at, recorded_at: string // ISO 8601; recorded_at not in identity\n../annals/README.md:35:  producer: { tool, version? },    // who wrote it; (tool, kind) names a vocabulary\n../annals/README.md:36:  meta?: { ... },                  // producer-owned metadata, uninterpreted\n../annals/README.md-37-  stream?: { id, seq, parent? },   // grouping + ordering, e.g. a conversation\n../annals/README.md-38-  links?: [{ rel, target }],       // typed edges to other records\n../annals/README.md-39-  content: unknown,                // never interpreted by annals\n--\n../annals/README.md-42-```\n../annals/README.md-43-\n../annals/README.md-44-The envelope carries no downstream concepts: no actor, no model, no session.\n../annals/README.md:45:A vocabulary that wants them (cledger records who spoke and which model\n../annals/README.md-46-served a turn) puts them in `meta`. Each field answers exactly two\n../annals/README.md-47-store-level questions — is it in the id, and does redaction walk it:\n../annals/README.md-48-\n../annals/README.md-49-| field | in identity | redaction-walked |\n../annals/README.md-50-|---|---|---|\n../annals/README.md:51:| kind, occurred_at, stream, media_type, content, links | yes | content yes |\n../annals/README.md-52-| meta | **no** | **no** — provenance only, never free text |\n../annals/README.md-53-| raw | no | yes (`raw.data`) |\n../annals/README.md:54:| producer, context, recorded_at, redactions | no | no |\n../annals/README.md-55-| resolved | no | **no** — never put payloads here |\n../annals/README.md-56-\n../annals/README.md-57-`meta` being identity-excluded is the point: provenance can be added or\n../annals/README.md-58-enriched later without the same fact getting a new id. It is not\n../annals/README.md-59-redaction-walked — the contract is structured provenance only (ids, names,\n../annals/README.md-60-labels); anything that could carry source text or a secret belongs in\n../annals/README.md:61:`content`/`raw`. This matches the pre-extraction behavior (actor/producer\n../annals/README.md-62-were never walked) and keeps UUID-heavy metadata out of the entropy scan's\n../annals/README.md:63:false-positive path. A vocabulary that\n../annals/README.md-64-needs one of its facts *in* identity puts it in `content`. Note the standing\n../annals/README.md:65:consequence: two records differing only by producer or meta dedup to one —\n../annals/README.md-66-byte-identical content is the same fact.\n../annals/README.md-67-\n../annals/README.md-68-## Namespaces\n--\n../annals/README.md-72-(`refs/notes/<name>`), the state directory under `.git`, the config file\n../annals/README.md-73-name, and the CLI the pre-push hook invokes. Producers that want their own\n../annals/README.md-74-independently-pushable, independently-wipeable ref (a derived layer that must\n../annals/README.md:75:be rebuildable, say) open their own namespace; producers extending an\n../annals/README.md:76:existing vocabulary write into that vocabulary's namespace through its\n../annals/README.md-77-owner's API. cledger uses `{ name: \"conversation-ledger\", configFile: \".cledger.json\" }`.\n../annals/README.md-78-\n../annals/README.md-79-Two namespaces in one repo chain two hook blocks in `pre-push`. Git feeds\n--\n../annals/README.md-92-is the second reason not to smuggle payloads into other fields. Enforced\n../annals/README.md-93-softly: an event serializing over `limits.warnEventBytes` (default 5MB)\n../annals/README.md-94-warns on stderr but still appends — capture must never drop records on size\n../annals/README.md:95:alone; set `limits.maxEventBytes` to opt into hard refusal for a producer\n../annals/README.md-96-that would rather fail loudly, such as a derived layer.\n../annals/README.md-97-\n../annals/README.md-98-## Identity records (optional pattern)\n../annals/README.md-99-\n../annals/README.md-100-The envelope has no actor field, and attribution does not need one: an\n../annals/README.md:101:identity can be a record like any other — its own kind, its own producer —\n../annals/README.md-102-and a record claims authorship with a link (`{ rel: \"authored_by\", target:\n../annals/README.md-103-<identity record id> }`). That is how git-bug stores identities, versioned\n../annals/README.md-104-and signable, in the same store as its bugs. Nothing in annals mandates\n../annals/README.md:105:this; a vocabulary can just as well denormalize `meta.actor` onto every\n../annals/README.md-106-record (cledger does today) and adopt identity records later without a\n../annals/README.md:107:schema change — both are producer-space conventions.\n../annals/README.md-108-\n../annals/README.md-109-## Prior art\n../annals/README.md-110-\n../annals/README.md-111-[git-bug's `entity/dag`](https://github.com/git-bug/git-bug) (Go) is the\n../annals/README.md-112-closest relative — replicated append-only operations in git refs, id = hash\n../annals/README.md-113-of the serialized op, per-type `{namespace, typename, formatVersion}`; its\n../annals/README.md:114:identification triple matches annals' `(producer.tool, kind,\n../annals/README.md:115:producer.version)`. Dolt's git-remote support solves an overlapping problem\n../annals/README.md-116-with a versioned SQL database; it lacks commit anchoring, which is the\n../annals/README.md-117-mechanism everything here hangs off.\n--\n../conversation-ledger/docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md-4-\n../conversation-ledger/docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md-5-## Scope\n../conversation-ledger/docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md-6-\n../conversation-ledger/docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:7:Conversation Ledger defines conversation-specific vocabulary over Annals' canonical\n../conversation-ledger/docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md-8-append-only event format and git-backed storage protocol. It preserves exact visible\n../conversation-ledger/docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md-9-content while staying out of the working tree. Transport is on by default and rides normal git use:\n../conversation-ledger/docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md-10-a pre-push hook pushes the ledger ref alongside `git pu